---
import AcademyScene from "./AcademyScene.astro";
import PassportTools from "./PassportTools.astro";
import {roles,missionRoleBrief,missionFacts,recoveryProfiles,type MissionKind} from "../lib/mission-engine";
import {missionSummaries,missionGuides} from "../data/learner-guidance";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
import "../styles/learner-guidance.css";
interface Props {kind?:MissionKind}
const {kind="recovery"}=Astro.props;
const guide=missionSummaries[kind];
const facts=kind==="recovery"?missionFacts.recovery:missionFacts.a1;
const title=kind==="a1"?"The Sealed Workshop":kind==="a2"?"Restore the Relay":"Operation Last Light";
---
<section class="mission" data-mission={kind} aria-label={title+" playable trial"}>
 <header class="mission-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLAYABLE {kind==="recovery"?"FINAL MISSION":"ASSESSMENT"}</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{kind==="a1"?"Inspect. Remember. Reconstruct. Repair. Put four capabilities to work in an unfamiliar workshop.":kind==="a2"?"A silent relay, a faulty circuit and two competing records. Restore the signal through precise collaboration.":"The last intact research archive is inside Meridian Station. Recover it without losing what makes it worth recovering."}</p></div><span class="mission-seal" aria-hidden="true">M<br/>/27</span></header>
 <p class="learner-orientation"><strong>How to play:</strong> follow the Mission Journal. <strong>Go to this objective</strong> selects its role and room for you. Use that room’s labelled controls and read the result. You can complete every practical task, finish the trial and export its record inside full screen.</p>
 <AcademyScene room="meridian" mode="mission" contextId={'mission:'+kind} />
 <div data-immersive-panel="mission">
 <p data-legacy-mission hidden class="mission-status" role="status"></p>
 <section class="learner-guide" aria-label="Mission instructions">
  <p class="eyebrow">{kind==="recovery"?"FINAL PROJECT":"ASSESSMENT"} / PRACTICAL TRIAL</p>
  <h3>Your mission</h3><p>{guide.goal}</p>
  <p class="small">The trial is ready to play. Your actions save locally as you go. Solo practice allows role switching; pairs and teams can share a screen and rotate control.</p>
  <div class="learner-next">
   <p class="eyebrow" data-mission-next-label>DO THIS NEXT</p>
   <h4 data-mission-next-title>{kind==="recovery"?"First, preserve the plan you intend to test":kind==="a1"?"Inspect the arrival scene":"Restore the 6 V circuit"}</h4>
   <p data-mission-next-action>{kind==="recovery"?"At Dispatch, use Coordinator. Write an initial sequence naming your route, the evidence you need and who checks it. Select Preserve this plan version.":missionGuides[kind==="a1"?"observe":"circuit"].action}</p>
   <p class="small" data-mission-next-success>{kind==="recovery"?"Done when Version 1 appears in the preserved plan history.":"Done when: "+missionGuides[kind==="a1"?"observe":"circuit"].success}</p>
   <button type="button" data-mission-next disabled>Go to this objective</button>
  </div>
 </section>
 <div class="mission-setup"><label>Scenario for next trial<select data-scenario><option value="baseline">Baseline</option><option value="equipment-failure">Equipment failure</option><option value="conflicting-archive">Conflicting archive</option></select></label><label hidden={kind!=="recovery"}>Declared recovery objective<select data-objective><option value="physical">Recover physical archive</option><option value="digital">Recover verified digital copy</option><option value="stabilise">Stabilise for handover</option></select></label><button type="button" data-start-mission disabled>Start new trial</button><span class="small">Changing Scenario takes effect when you select Start new trial. Saved trials resume automatically; starting over keeps completed records. For a new final-project run, choose its objective before the first practical action.</span></div>
 <div class="mission-rolebar" role="group" aria-label="Choose your role">{Object.entries(roles).map(([id,r])=><button type="button" data-role={id} disabled aria-pressed={id==="observer"}>{r.title}</button>)}</div>
 <details class="role-brief" open><summary data-role-title>Observer / Navigator briefing</summary><p data-role-brief>{missionRoleBrief("observer",kind)}</p><p class="small" data-role-tools></p><a href="#role-packs">Read all role packs</a></details>
 <div class="mission-grid">
  <aside class="mission-objectives"><p class="eyebrow">MISSION JOURNAL</p><h3>Required objectives</h3><p data-mission-progress class="small"></p><details class="learner-checklist" open><summary>All objectives and instructions</summary><ol data-objectives></ol></details><p class="small">A tick records a practical condition met. It is not an academic grade. Changing equipment can reopen a dependent objective.</p></aside>
  <div class="mission-console">
   <nav class="zone-tabs" aria-label="Station areas">
    {[["arrival","01 Arrival"],["workshop","02 Workshop"],["power","03 Power bay"],["control","04 Control room"],["archive","05 Archive"],["dispatch","06 Dispatch"]].map(([id,label])=><button type="button" data-zone={id} disabled>{label}</button>)}
   </nav>
   <h3 class="learner-console-title">Room controls and feedback</h3>
   <p role="status" data-mission-status class="mission-status">Your saved mission is loading. The instructions and role packs are available below.</p>
   <section data-zone-panel="arrival"><p class="learner-role-note">Use Observer / Navigator for all three tasks in this room.</p><p class="eyebrow">OBSERVATION · MEMORY · SPATIAL REASONING</p><h3>The room is your first instrument.</h3><p>Inspect the five supplied objects, then close the manifest before reconstructing its order. Match the north arrow to the room rather than the camera.</p><div class="actions">{["lens","spool","tile","map","manifest"].map(item=><button type="button" data-inspect={item}>Inspect {item}</button>)}</div><p data-inspection class="inspection-note"></p><button type="button" data-hide-manifest>Hide inspection notes</button><form data-recall><label>Recall the packing order<input name="items" autocomplete="off" placeholder="item, item, item" required maxlength="100"/></label><button>Check recall</button></form><form data-orient><label>Clockwise rotation of north<select name="degrees"><option value="0">0°</option><option value="90">90°</option><option value="180">180°</option><option value="270">270°</option></select></label><button>Test orientation</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="workshop" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Systems Specialist to change gears, release the brake and turn the crank.</p><p class="eyebrow">MECHANICAL DIAGNOSIS</p><h3>The recovery cradle.</h3><p data-cradle-instruction>{kind==="recovery"?"A twelve-tooth driver must match the verified archive profile. Investigator verifies A for one-third output (36 teeth) or B for one-quarter output (48 teeth); Systems releases the brake and tests that setup.":"A twelve-tooth input gear drives the cam. The cradle requires half-speed output in the opposite direction. Inspect the interlock before applying another turn."}</p><p data-profile-status class="inspection-note" hidden={kind!=="recovery"}>Verify the archive profile in the Control room before testing the final cradle.</p><label>Follower gear<select data-follower><option value="36">36 teeth</option><option value="24">24 teeth</option><option value="48">48 teeth</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-brake/> Release the holding brake</label><button type="button" data-turn>Turn input once</button><output data-mechanism-readout></output></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="power" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Systems Specialist. Measure the original fault before replacing it.</p><p class="eyebrow">ELECTRONICS · MEASUREMENT</p><h3>A complete path.</h3><p>The training supply is 6 V. Power flows through the fuse, switch, lamp and return. Find the break before replacing anything.</p><button type="button" data-measure>Measure supply and fuse</button><output data-measurement></output><label>Fuse condition<select data-fuse><option value="open">Open fuse</option><option value="intact">Intact fuse</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-switch/> Close the load switch</label><p data-circuit-readout></p></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="control" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Investigator for the archive comparison and permission repair.</p><p class="eyebrow">DIGITAL INVESTIGATION · PERMISSIONS</p><h3>Which copy can you justify?</h3><div data-archive-records></div><form data-replica><label>Copy matching the current signed source<select name="replica"><option value="A">Archive A</option><option value="B">Archive B</option></select></label><button>Verify selected archive</button></form><details open><summary>Fictional application: permission defect</summary><p>Observer/read is allowed. Technician/service is allowed. Registrar/certify is allowed. A defective rule also grants observer/certify.</p><form data-policy><label>Subject<select name="subject"><option value="observer">Observer</option><option value="technician">Technician</option><option value="registrar">Registrar</option></select></label><label>Action<select name="action"><option value="certify">Certify</option><option value="read">Read</option><option value="service">Service</option></select></label><label>New decision<select name="decision"><option value="deny">Deny</option><option value="allow">Allow</option></select></label><button>Apply policy and run checks</button></form></details></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="archive" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">{kind==="a2"?"Use Coordinator to complete the three handoff fields. Agreement and route are final-project tasks.":"Use Coordinator for agreement and handoff; switch to Observer / Navigator for the route."}</p><p class="eyebrow">COMMUNICATION · NEGOTIATION · NAVIGATION</p><h3>An agreement that can be acted on.</h3><blockquote>“Preserve the original. Tell me who receives the archive. Then we can agree a recovery.”<cite>— Meridian custodian</cite></blockquote><form data-agreement><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve"/> Commit to preserving the original</label><label>Named handover recipient<input name="recipient" maxlength="100" placeholder="Name or assigned team role" required/></label><button>Negotiate handling agreement</button></form><form data-handoff><label>Item<select name="item"><option value="archive">Archive</option><option value="verified archive">Verified archive</option></select></label><label>Destination<select name="destination"><option value="workshop">Workshop</option><option value="dispatch">Dispatch</option></select></label><label>Condition<select name="condition"><option value="immediately">Immediately</option><option value="after integrity check">After integrity check</option></select></label><button>Send structured handoff</button></form><h4>Route model</h4><p>Upper and lift routes depend on the lift supply. The service passage is independent and includes two marked sensor pauses. Consult the scenario bulletin before committing.</p><p data-disruption class="scenario-bulletin"></p><form data-route><label>Route<select name="route"><option value="upper">Upper passage</option><option value="service">Service passage</option><option value="lift">Lift</option></select></label><button>Test route dependencies</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="dispatch" hidden><details data-mission-plan-notes open={kind==="recovery"}><summary>{kind==="recovery"?"Your original plan and revisions":"Optional planning notes and preserved versions"}</summary><p class="learner-role-note">Use Coordinator to preserve your plan versions. Any role can finish once the required objectives are met.</p><p class="eyebrow">PLANNING · ADAPTATION · DEFENCE</p><h3>Keep the decisions, including the ones you changed.</h3><p>Record an original plan before your revision. A revision should explain a new observation, a tested assumption or a changed condition. Earlier versions remain intact.</p><form data-plan><label>Plan or revision<textarea name="text" rows="4" minlength="20" maxlength="8000" required placeholder="Route, evidence, responsibilities, and why this version makes sense…"></textarea></label><button>Preserve this plan version</button></form><div data-plans></div></details>{kind==="recovery"&&<section class="resolution-evidence" aria-label="Evidence for your chosen ending"><h4>Evidence for your chosen ending</h4><p>Complete the eleven common objectives, then record the evidence for the outcome you intend to resolve. These checks confirm the record is present and matches the model; your written defence explains its quality.</p><form data-resolution-evidence><label>Outcome to document<select name="ending" data-outcome-choice><option value="physical">Physical recovery</option><option value="digital">Verified digital recovery</option><option value="stabilise">Stabilisation and handover</option></select></label><label>Responsible recipient<input name="recipient" required minlength="2" maxlength="100" placeholder="Named custodian or receiving role"/></label><fieldset data-outcome-fields="physical"><legend>Physical custody and support</legend><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="support" required/> I confirm the verified profile's cradle and selected route have been tested for this transfer.</label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve-physical" required/> I acknowledge original-preserving custody with the named recipient.</label></fieldset><fieldset data-outcome-fields="digital" hidden><legend>Verified receipt and retained original</legend><p data-digital-receipt>Read the verified profile's receipt in the Control room.</p><label>Verified receipt code<input name="receipt" maxlength="100" required/></label><label>Original retained at<input name="digital-location" minlength="3" maxlength="100" required placeholder="Recorded station location"/></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve-digital" required/> I confirm the original remains preserved at this location.</label></fieldset><fieldset data-outcome-fields="stabilise" hidden><legend>Stable handover and remaining work</legend><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="stable" required/> I confirm the tested equipment supports a stable archive pending handover.</label><label>Stable archive location<input name="stable-location" minlength="3" maxlength="100" required/></label><label>Remaining limitation and next responsibility<textarea name="limitation" minlength="20" maxlength="2000" rows="3" required placeholder="What remains unresolved and what must the recipient do next?"></textarea></label></fieldset><button>Record outcome evidence</button></form><p data-outcome-status role="status">No outcome evidence recorded yet.</p></section>}
   <h4>{kind==="recovery"?"Resolve the recovery":"Complete the trial"}</h4><div class="ending-choices">{kind==="recovery"?<><button type="button" data-ending="physical">Recover physical archive</button><button type="button" data-ending="digital">Recover verified digital copy</button><button type="button" data-ending="stabilise">Stabilise for documented handover</button></>:<button type="button" data-ending={kind==="a1"?"physical":"digital"}>Finish {kind==="a1"?"workshop":"relay"} trial</button>}</div><p>No ending is an academic grade. Complete the trial's required capabilities before resolving it.</p></section>
  </div>
 </div>
 <section data-debrief data-immersive-reflection hidden class="mission-debrief"><p class="eyebrow">AFTER ACTION</p><h3 data-ending-title></h3><p data-ending-text></p><p>{guide.after}</p>{kind==="recovery"&&<p><a href={withBase("/sessions/week-12/#training-title-12")}>Continue to the Week 12 after-action account</a>. Your run stays saved; opening another page leaves full screen.</p>}<p>Now explain your observations and decisions using the exported action record. Compare a different scenario: which skill transferred, which assumption changed, and what remains uncertain?</p></section>
 <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-export-mission disabled>Export assessment record</button><button type="button" data-print-mission disabled>Print mission report</button></div>
 <details><summary>Action record and previous runs</summary><ol data-action-log></ol><div data-run-comparison></div></details>
 <section id="role-packs"><h3>Four roles. One shared operation.</h3><p>Use one browser, share a screen or rotate control. Solo students switch roles. Local role selections record practice responsibility, not verified identity.</p><div class="role-packs">{Object.entries(roles).map(([id,r])=><details><summary>{r.title}</summary><p>{missionRoleBrief(id as keyof typeof roles,kind)}</p><p>{r.tools.join(" · ")}</p></details>)}</div></section>
 <details><summary>Static mission worksheet and sample approach</summary><p>Assign the roles above. Packing order: {facts.order.join(", ")}. The map rotates north {facts.orientation}° clockwise. Inspect all five objects and predict before checking. The circuit needs an intact fuse and a closed switch; measure its 6 V supply first.</p>
 {kind==="recovery"?<><p>Verify the archive before configuring its cradle. Baseline and Equipment Failure use signed source M27-A and complete Archive A: profile A requires a 12:36 gear ratio for one-third output. Conflicting Archive uses signed revision M27-B and complete Archive B: profile B requires 12:48 for one-quarter output. Release the holding brake and test the matched gear.</p><p>The verified profile must support the cradle test, Coordinator's handoff and route test. Remove observer/certify while preserving legitimate access. Agree to preserve the original and name the recipient. Send “verified archive → dispatch → after integrity check”. Equipment Failure disables upper and lift routes; the service route remains available. Preserve the first plan and an explained revision.</p><p>Record your chosen ending's evidence. Physical: name the recipient and acknowledge tested cradle/route support and original-preserving custody. Digital: record the matching receipt ({recoveryProfiles.A.receipt} for A; {recoveryProfiles.B.receipt} for B), recipient, retained original's location and preservation. Stabilisation: name the recipient and location, confirm the tested stable state, and explain remaining work. Attach this record to the common mission evidence and justify the choice in your written account.</p></>:<><p>The cradle uses a 12:24 gear ratio and a released brake. The baseline signed source is M27-A; Archive A matches. In Conflicting Archive a later signed source M27-B supersedes it and Archive B matches. Remove observer/certify while preserving legitimate access, and communicate “verified archive → dispatch → after integrity check”.</p><p>A1 checks inspection, ordered recall, orientation and cradle preparation. A2 checks circuit diagnosis, archive selection, permission repair and precise handoff. Use the assessment brief's lab evidence table for detailed checks and changed-condition work.</p></>}
 <p>These are published teaching rules. An ending is practical evidence; an explanation's quality is assessed by a person.</p></details>
 <PassportTools />
 <dialog data-restart-dialog><h2>Start a new trial?</h2><p>The current in-progress trial will be replaced. Completed records and your lab passport remain. Export this run first if you need its unfinished record.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-restart-confirm>Start new trial</button><button type="button" data-restart-cancel>Keep this trial</button></div></dialog>
 <pre class="mission-print-report" hidden data-mission-print></pre>
 </div>
 <noscript><p>The complete mission worksheet and role information above remain available. For interactive play, enable JavaScript or use the campus pack.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>import "../scripts/mission-client";</script>